Node.js documentation site
==========================

The GitHub Pages workflow .github/workflows/klipper3d-deploy.yaml uses Node.js
26.9+ (26.x) and host/package-lock.json. Python, pip and MkDocs are not required.
The site configuration and navigation are in site.yml; docs/CNAME continues
to control the custom domain. No deployment is performed by local builds.

Install dependencies, then build the English site from the repository root:

  npm ci --prefix host --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund
  node scripts/build-docs.ts /tmp/klipper-docs-preview

Build all active languages (fetches the official translations into a temporary
checkout, then cleans only that checkout):

  docs/_klipper3d/build-website.sh /tmp/klipper-docs-all

For an offline build, provide an existing klipper-translations checkout:

  docs/_klipper3d/build-website.sh /tmp/klipper-docs-all /path/to/klipper-translations

The output directory must be new and outside docs/. Sources and existing sites
are never overwritten. A failed build may leave partial output; do not publish
it. The default output is repository-root/site. The workflow deploys only after
a successful build. Serve generated output over HTTP using a static server;
file:// cannot fetch the search index. No Python HTTP server is needed.

Translation builds use active_translations and Navigation.md and prefer
manual-index.md. Each language has its own navigation and search index. Search
supports literal Unicode words, title ranking, live results, highlighting and
shareable queries. It deliberately does not apply language-specific stemming:
technical identifiers and Chinese substrings remain literal.

Rendering decisions:
- Preserve existing ASCII heading anchors and two-space child-list indentation.
- Preserve code examples rather than reproducing the old hook's code rewriting.
- Use CommonMark fenced code inside lists instead of the old inline-code result.
- Blank lines may separate paragraphs within one unordered list rather than
  splitting it into multiple lists; item order, nesting and content remain.
- Styling is local and responsive, with system light/dark colors; the former
  Material theme and its analytics integration are not loaded.

Validation and benchmarks (Node only):

  node --test --test-isolation=none --test-concurrency=1 host/test/docs-*.test.ts
  node host/bench/docs-render.ts
  node host/bench/docs-search.ts
  node host/bench/docs-translations.ts /path/to/klipper-translations

Fixed old-renderer references remain in host/contracts/. These are evidence,
not an executable Python dependency. Real GitHub Actions deployment and public
site acceptance must still follow the repository PR and release process.
